{"kind":"stack","id":"moon-stack","title":"The Moon's Movement Relative to the Earth","theme":{"background":"#0b1d3a","foreground":"#ffffff","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Orbit"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"The path the Moon follows as it travels around the Earth. It takes about 27 days to complete one orbit."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Rotation"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"When an object spins around its own centre. The Earth rotates once every 24 hours, which gives us day and night."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"What does the Moon travel around?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"The Sun","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"The Earth","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Mars","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"About how long does the Moon take to orbit the Earth once?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"About 1 day","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"About 27 days","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"About 365 days","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-d","label":"About 7 days","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"A pupil is asked to draw the Moon's path. Which should they choose?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Draw a circle around the Earth","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Draw a straight line past the Earth","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"Well done! The Moon moves in a rough circle, called an orbit, around the Earth."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"Not quite. The Moon does not fly off in a straight line. Its path curves around the Earth."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Why do we always see the same side of the Moon from Earth?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"The Moon does not spin at all","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"The Moon spins once for each orbit","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"The Moon only spins at night","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Is the Moon's orbit around the Earth bigger or smaller than the Earth itself?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Smaller","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"end"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Bigger","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"end"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"end","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"end-h","content":"You finished the Moon's movement quiz!"},{"type":"text","id":"end-m","content":"Great work. Remember: the Moon orbits the Earth, and it takes about 27 days to go all the way round."}],"actions":[]}}
